 msgid "Hades lifts the darkest parts of the film to the black level that the display gives for Low-Latency in its Dolby Vision information, so that they are not crushed into its black: the darkest parts rise the most, brighter ones less, and the highlights not at all. Most OLED TVs give 0, and nothing changes; LCD TVs and projectors give about 0.005 to 0.27 cd/m². On a display whose real black is lower than the one it gives (some LCD TVs with local dimming), blacks then look grey: turn this off. Not used while 'Low-Latency: peak and colours set here' is on, which has its own black. Takes effect from the next video."
 msgstr ""
 
+#. Hades: label of setting "videoplayer.hadesupscalerhd"; translated in Estuary (#34060)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42060"
+msgid "Upscaler for videos of 1080p and above"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: help of setting "videoplayer.hadesupscalerhd"; translated in Estuary (#34061)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42061"
+msgid "For experts. How videos of 1080p and above are scaled up to a larger screen, such as a 4K TV. Off (the default): Kodi's own scaling, as always. The others redraw the picture with a shader that rebuilds fine detail, so the picture changes: edges and fine lines come out sharper and closer to a picture made at the larger size, as measured on films and animation. RAVU is the lightest. FSRCNNX 8 gives more detail and needs a mid-range graphics card. FSRCNNX 16 gives the most and needs a strong one, not a small integrated chip. If your graphics card cannot draw it in time, it is turned off for that video and a message says so. Used only where the video is drawn more than 1.3 times its size in width and height (1.41 for RAVU), such as 1080p on a 4K screen. Not used for Dolby Vision. Applies at once."
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: label of setting "videoplayer.hadesupscalersd"; translated in Estuary (#34062)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42062"
+msgid "Upscaler for videos below 1080p"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: help of setting "videoplayer.hadesupscalersd"; translated in Estuary (#34063)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42063"
+msgid "For experts. The same choice for smaller videos (720p, DVD and other standard definition), which are scaled up the most. Off (the default): Kodi's own scaling. RAVU is the lightest; FSRCNNX 8 and 16 rebuild more detail and ask more of the graphics card. They change the picture. Used only where the video is drawn more than 1.3 times its size in width and height (1.41 for RAVU). Not used for Dolby Vision. Applies at once."
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: label of setting "videoplayer.hadesupscaleranime"; translated in Estuary (#34064)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42064"
+msgid "Upscaler for animation"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: help of setting "videoplayer.hadesupscaleranime"; translated in Estuary (#34065)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42065"
+msgid "For experts. A separate choice for animation and anime, used when the genre of the video, from your library or from the add-on that plays it, says Animation or Anime. \"Same as the other two\" (the default) keeps the two choices above. Choose one here to use it for animation instead, for instance a stronger one for anime while other videos keep a lighter one or Kodi's scaling. Applies at once."
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: value of the upscaler settings: off; translated in Estuary (#34066)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42066"
+msgid "Off (Kodi's scaling)"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: value of the upscaler settings: RAVU lite; translated in Estuary (#34067)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42067"
+msgid "RAVU (light)"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: value of the upscaler settings: FSRCNNX x2 8-0-4-1; translated in Estuary (#34068)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42068"
+msgid "FSRCNNX 8 (more detail)"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: value of the upscaler settings: FSRCNNX x2 16-0-4-1; translated in Estuary (#34069)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42069"
+msgid "FSRCNNX 16 (most detail)"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: value of setting "videoplayer.hadesupscaleranime": the other two decide; translated in Estuary (#34070)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42070"
+msgid "Same as the other two"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: title of the message when the upscaler is turned off because it is too slow; translated in Estuary (#34072)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42072"
+msgid "Upscaler turned off"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: text of the message when the upscaler is turned off because it is too slow; translated in Estuary (#34073)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#42073"
+msgid "Your graphics card could not draw it in time for this video, so Kodi's own scaling is used."
+msgstr ""
