@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# The upscalers of LibreELEC Hades
+
+These are the shaders that the expert settings *Upscaler for videos of 1080p and above*, *Upscaler for videos
+below 1080p* and *Upscaler for animation* (Player > Videos) draw with: mpv user shaders, which libplacebo reads
+(`pl_mpv_user_shader_parse()`) and the Dolby Vision bridge of LibreELEC Hades draws with a picture
+(`tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_upscale.c`). They are off by default.
+
+Each file is kept byte for byte as its author publishes it, with its notice. They are separate files, read when a
+video is drawn with them; nothing of them is compiled into Kodi.
+
+| File | What | Origin | Version | SHA256 | Licence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `ravu-lite-ar-r4.hook` | RAVU lite, radius 4, anti-ringing: a luma doubler | https://github.com/bjin/mpv-prescalers (Bin Jin) | commit `b3f0a59d68f33b7162051ea5970a5169558f0ea2` (2024-01-11) | `2e7c9beb79be10c57c85eede7a4b6ba1f031a97a26170d88450fc4330a5e8408` | LGPL-3.0-or-later (the file's notice, and the repository's `LICENSE`) |
+| `FSRCNNX_x2_8-0-4-1.glsl` | FSRCNNX x2, 8 filters: a luma doubler | https://github.com/igv/FSRCNN-TensorFlow (igv), release `1.1` | the release asset `FSRCNNX_x2_8-0-4-1.glsl` (published 2017-11-09) | `e800dbc5c1c95185cc82216c597724533ff5f2880179f256eef600f03e8dc2ae` | LGPL-3.0-or-later (the file's notice; the repository's code, which makes such files, is MIT) |
+| `FSRCNNX_x2_16-0-4-1.glsl` | FSRCNNX x2, 16 filters: a luma doubler | the same, release `1.1` | the release asset `FSRCNNX_x2_16-0-4-1.glsl` (published 2017-11-09) | `d5a24a271e5d9a3f7f7a053b150c460a44c25b3cf7f770857d57cc3a2e1c9965` | LGPL-3.0-or-later (the file's notice) |
+
+The texts of the licence are beside them: `LICENSE-LGPL-3.0.txt`, and `LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt`, as the LGPL is
+version 3 of the GPL with additional permissions (in the source tree, `LICENSES/LGPL-3.0-or-later` and
+`LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later`). Kodi is GPL-2.0-or-later, and the Kodi of LibreELEC
+Hades is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later (`LICENSES/README.md`), with which these files are compatible; they
+are not compatible with GPL-2.0-only.
+
+## How they were chosen
+
+Measured on the host with libplacebo's renderer (the libplacebo of the build, with its patches) on Mesa's
+software OpenGL ES 3.1: frames of a film (two UHD Blu-ray samples) and of an anime episode, made smaller (bicubic,
+and a box filter) and drawn back at their size, compared with the original (PSNR and SSIM of the luma, and Delta E
+ITP for HDR10), against Kodi's Lanczos 3:
+
+- RAVU lite: nearer to the original at the edges (+0.1 to +1.3 dB of PSNR), about the same elsewhere, at 2 to
+  3 times the GPU work of Lanczos 3;
+- FSRCNNX 8: much nearer at the edges (+0.3 to +3.4 dB), at 5 to 13 times;
+- FSRCNNX 16: the nearest of all, on film, animation and HDR10 (+0.4 to +4.7 dB), at 14 to 38 times.
+
+Their shaders run only where the picture is drawn larger than that (their own `//!WHEN` lines): RAVU above 1.41
+times its size in width and height, FSRCNNX above 1.3 times. LibreELEC Hades asks for an upscaler only there.
+
+Not taken, by the same measurements: FSR 1 with or without RCAS (AMD, MIT), Anime4K (bloc97, MIT), NNEDI3 (Bin
+Jin, LGPL-3.0-or-later), the EWA filters of libplacebo. ArtCNN (MIT) needs compute shaders, which libplacebo's
+OpenGL ES backend does not give.
